# React Aria Components (RAC)

- Build accessible, unstyled components via composition (slots + React context), not deep one-off prop trees.
- Reuse `react-aria` / `react-stately` hooks; RAC should be the DOM composition layer, not a second behavior implementation.
- Preserve render-prop / context patterns used by neighboring components (`*Context`, slot providers).
- Keep styling concerns out — consumers (including S2) supply classes/styles.
- Public props and contexts are part of the semver surface; update types and docs with API changes.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — compose hooks + slots
// use existing Button/Dialog patterns in this package as the template

// ❌ BAD — hard-coding Spectrum tokens or duplicating useDialog logic inline
```
